1.Aim

To write and execute a Python program to demonstrate list and it's related functions

2.Algorithm

1.Start the program.
2.Create a list containing the elements [150, 40, 90, 10, 100, 50].
3.Find and display the length of the list using the len() function.
4.Add the element 140 to the end of the list using append().
5.Insert the element 200 at index 1 using insert().
6.Remove the element 10 from the list using remove().
7.Remove the last element from the list using pop().
8.Count the number of occurrences of 40 using count().
9.Find the index position of 90 using index().
10.Arrange the elements in ascending order using sort().
11.Reverse the order of the elements using reverse().
12.Create a copy of the list using copy().
13.Add the elements 30 and 11 to the list using extend().
14.Find and display the largest element using max().
15.Find and display the smallest element using min().
16.Calculate and display the sum of all elements using sum().
17.Remove all elements from the list using clear().
18.Display the cleared list.
19.Stop the program

3.Source Code

list = [150,40,90,10,100,50]
a= len(list)
print ("The length of the string:",a)
list.append(140)
print("The element added is:",list)
list.insert(1,200)
print ("After insertion:",list)
list.remove(10)
print ("After deletion:",list)
list.pop()
print ("After popping element:",list)
b = list.count(40)
print("After count:",b)
c = list.index(90)
print("The index is:",c)
list.sort()
print("The sorted list is:",list)
list.reverse()
print("The reversed list is:",list)
new_list = list.copy()
print("The copied list is:",list)
list.extend([30,11])
print("The extended list is:",list)
d= max(list)
print("The greatest element is:",d)
e= min(list)
print("The smallest element is:",e)
f = sum(list)
print("The sum of list is:",f)
list.clear()
print("The cleared list is:",list)

